ble date 07  December 2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  USD 102  USD 102  Annual cost impact (*)  1.07%  0.21%   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  1.02% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  USD 102  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  USD 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of your investment per year.  USD 0  Transaction costs  0%  USD 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  USD 0   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 05 December 2030, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\nThe index sponsor makes no representation whatsoever as to the advisability of purchasing the product and does not sponsor, promote or endorse the product in any manner.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "7326a439-99a9-4cbc-822d-ecd265a337f4", "name": "CE14812LBH-7D70D-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "c3f21b89-73d0-4e84-bcf7-ccc022920956", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543679_07bd9899_CE14812LBH-7D70D-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2641, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191982969  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  21 February 2026 07:47:10 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying shares (each share, an Underlying). The product may also pay coupon under predefined conditions in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If a Barrier Event has not occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount.\\n2.  If  a  Barrier  Event  has  occurred:  delivery  of  the  number  of  shares  of  the  WorstPerforming Underlying (as determined below) plus a payment in cash in respect of any fraction of a share. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price of at least one Underlying is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n\\nThe Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n- The number of shares of an underlying is the Notional Amount per certificate divided by its Initial Reference Price converted, if necessary, into the Product Currency using the applicable exchange rate on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  20 November 2025  Issue Date  04 December 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  22 November 2027  Redemption Date (maturity)  29 November 2027  Coupon Valuation Date(s)  20 February 2026, 20 May 2026, 20 August  2026, 20 November 2026, 22 February 2027,  20 May 2027, 20 August 2027 and 22  November 2027  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  65% of the Initial Reference Price  Barrier  65% of the Initial Reference Price  Early Redemption Date(s)  06 March 2026, 03 June 2026, 03 September  2026, 04 December 2026, 08 March 2027,  03 June 2027 and 03 September 2027   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  CHF  Notional Amount (per certificate)  CHF 1,000   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n06 March 2026, 03 June 2026, 03 September\\n\\n2026, 04 December 2026, 08 March 2027,\\n\\n03 June 2027, 03 September 2027 and 29\\n\\nNovember 2027\\n\\n1.50% of the Notional Amount\\n\\n20 February 2026, 20 May 2026, 20 August\\n\\n2026, 20 November 2026, 22 February 2027,\\n\\n20 May 2027 and 20 August 2027\\n\\n100%, 95%, 90%, 85%, 80%, 75% and 70%\\n\\nof the Initial Reference Price\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE14812LBH\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE14812LBH-7D70D-EN.pdf.\\n\\nCoupon: A conditional coupon is due for payment at the relevant Conditional Coupon Rate each time the following condition (Coupon Condition) is met: if, on a Coupon Valuation Date,  the  closing  price  of  each  underlying  is  greater  than  or  equal  to  the  relevant Conditional Coupon Barrier. Otherwise, the coupon is missed but not lost definitely. All missed coupons will accumulate and become payable only if the Coupon Condition is subsequently satisfied.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to the relevant Autocall Barrier, the product will be redeemed  on  the  corresponding  Early  Redemption  Date.  You  will  receive  for  each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\nCoupon Payment Date(s)\\n\\nConditional Coupon Rate(s)\\n\\nAutocall Valuation Date(s)\\n\\nAutocall Barrier(s)\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  ISIN  BP PLC  BP/ LN  GB0007980591  TotalEnergies SE  TTE FP  FR0000120271  SLB Ltd  SLB UN  AN8068571086   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a short term investment horizon (less than three years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 1 out of 7, which is the lowest risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a very low level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  CHF 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  CHF 10,140  (product ends after 06 March  2026)  Average return  1.4%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  CHF 10,140  (product ends after 06 March  2026)  Average return  1.4%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  CHF 10,140  (product ends after 06 March  2026)  Average return  1.4%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  CHF 10,140  (product ends after 06 March  2026)  Average return  1.4%   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nthe amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- CHF 10,000 is invested\\n\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment CHF 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 06 March  2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  CHF 227  CHF 227  Annual cost impact (*)  2.36%  1.31%   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n(*) This illustrates how costs reduce your return each year over the holding period. For example it shows that if you exit at maturity your average return per year is projected to be 2.1% before costs and 0.78% after costs.\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  2.27% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  CHF 227  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  CHF 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of your investment per year.  CHF 0  Transaction costs  0%  CHF 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  CHF 0   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 29 November 2027, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "95f50cc3-9215-4d85-b4c8-81efa274083f", "name": "CE17205EBF-F0090-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "60daf191-9925-4551-b916-342ab62f5703", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543682_ca0c14ae_CE17205EBF-F0090-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2220, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Option  ISIN  XS3191926032  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  19 November 2025 00:25:21 CET   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has a full capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of an underlying index.\\n\\nOn the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate:\\n\\n1. If the Final Reference Price is less than or equal to 100% of the Initial Reference Price: a payment in cash equal to 100% of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price is above the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Initial Reference Price is the closing price of the Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price is the closing price of the Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  17 November 2025  Issue Date  24 November 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  17 November 2028  Redemption Date (maturity)  24 November 2028  Barrier  105% of the Initial Reference Price   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  EUR  Notional Amount (per certificate)  EUR 1,000   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| ## Underlying  ## Bloomberg Code  MSCI Singapore Free Index  SIMSCI   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a medium term investment horizon (three to five years).\\n- seek to invest in a capital growth product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- seek protection of the Notional Amount at maturity.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n2. If the Final Reference Price is greater than 100% of the Initial Reference Price:\\n- a.  If  a  Barrier  Event  has  occurred:  a  payment  in  cash  equal  to  114.65%  of  the Notional Amount\\n- b.  If  a  Barrier  Event  has  not  occurred:  a  payment  in  cash  equal  to  the  Notional Amount increased by the Performance of the Underlying.\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE17205EBF\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE17205EBF-F0090-EN.pdf.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 2 out of 7, which is a low risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a low level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nYou are entitled to receive back at least 100% of your capital (capital means Notional Amount). Any amount over this, and any additional return, depends on future market performance and is uncertain. However, this protection against future market performance will not apply if you cash-in before maturity.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  5 years  Example Investment  EUR 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit after 5  years  Minimum  EUR 10,000. The return is only guaranteed if you hold the product to maturity.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 9,362  EUR 10,000  Average return each year  -6.38%  0.0%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 9,490  EUR 10,000  Average return each year  -5.1%  0.0%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 10,053  EUR 11,465  Average return each year  0.53%  4.66%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 10,454  EUR 11,465  Average return each year  4.54%  4.66%   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference asset's past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- In the first year you would get back the amount that you invested (0% annual return). For the other holding periods we have assumed the product performs as shown in the moderate scenario\\n- EUR 10,000 is invested.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n| Investment EUR 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit after 5 years  Total costs  EUR 289  EUR 239  Annual cost impact (*)  2.96%  0.85%   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n(*) This illustrates how costs reduce your return each year over the holding period. For example it shows that if you exit at the recommended holding period your average return per year is projected to be 5.51% before costs and 4.66% after costs.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  2.39% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  EUR 239  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  EUR 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  EUR 0  Transaction costs  0%  EUR 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  EUR 0   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 24 November 2028, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\nThe index sponsor makes no representation whatsoever as to the advisability of purchasing the product and does not sponsor, promote or endorse the product in any manner.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "a90b617e-4167-4bdd-8d59-719c6d723f51", "name": "CE18209EBF-D883F-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "94235f46-6781-4e80-9e54-c4640f219bc6", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543726_22a228e6_CE18209EBF-D883F-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2502, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191939795  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  28 February 2026 11:30:19 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n- OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying  shares  (each  share,  an  Underlying).  The  product  will  also  pay  coupon  in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If a Barrier Event has not occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price of at least one Underlying is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the opening price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n- The number of shares of an underlying is the Notional Amount per certificate divided by 75% of its Initial Reference Price converted, if necessary, into the Product Currency using the applicable exchange rate on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  18 November 2025  Issue Date  02 December 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  02 December 2026  Redemption Date (maturity)  09 December 2026  Coupon Payment Date(s)  09 March 2026, 09 June 2026, 10 September  2026 and 09 December 2026  Barrier  65% of the Initial Reference Price  Early Redemption Date(s)  09 March 2026, 09 June 2026 and 10  September 2026   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nIssue Price\\n\\nProduct Currency\\n\\nNotional Amount (per certificate)\\n\\n100%\\n\\nUSD\\n\\nUSD 25,000\\n\\n| Coupon Rate(s)  3.2875% of the Notional Amount  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  02 March 2026, 02 June 2026 and 02  September 2026   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  ISIN  Agnico Eagle Mines Ltd  AEM UN  CA0084741085  Newmont Corp  NEM UN  US6516391066  Barrick Mining Corp  B UN  CA06849F1080   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\n2.  If  a  Barrier  Event  has  occurred:  delivery  of  the  number  of  shares  of  the  WorstPerforming Underlying (as determined below) plus a payment in cash in respect of any fraction of a share. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount. Coupon: A coupon is due for payment at the Coupon Rate on each Coupon Payment Date.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to 100% of its Initial Reference Price, the product will be redeemed on the corresponding Early Redemption Date. You will receive for each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE18209EBF\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE18209EBF-D883F-EN.pdf.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a short term investment horizon (less than three years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 1 out of 7, which is the lowest risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a very low level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  USD 1,273. The return is only guaranteed if you hold the product to maturity.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,002  (product ends after 09 March  2026)  Average return  0.02%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,002  (product ends after 09 March  2026)  Average return  0.02%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,002  (product ends after 09 March  2026)  Average return  0.02%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,002  (product ends after 09 March  2026)  Average return  0.02%   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- USD 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment USD 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 09 March  2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  USD 102  USD 102  Cost impact (*)  0.99%  0.99%   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n(*) This illustrates how costs reduce your return over the holding period. For example it shows that if you exit at maturity your average return is projected to be 1.02% before costs and 0.02% after costs.\\n\\nThis illustrates the effect of costs over a holding period of less than one year. This percentage cannot be directly compared to the cost impact figures provided for other PRIIPs.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  Recommended holding  period  Entry costs  1.02% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  USD 102  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  USD 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of your investment per year.  USD 0  Transaction costs  0%  USD 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  USD 0   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 09 December 2026, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "793509ff-3cc5-4e93-b11e-472885eac2d4", "name": "CE18416EBF-2F8EC-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "b6c79e13-f650-484d-9f00-a2077a06bd1d", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543730_75a48c29_CE18416EBF-2F8EC-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2223, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Option  ISIN  XS3191940538  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  19 November 2025 01:14:41 CET   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has a full capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of an underlying.\\n\\nOn the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate:\\n\\n1. If the Final Reference Price is less than or equal to 100% of the Initial Reference Price: a payment in cash equal to 100% of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Closing Price of the Underlying observed daily between the Barrier Start Date (excluded) and the Barrier End Date (included) is at least once above the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Initial Reference Price is the closing price of the Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price is the closing price of the Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  18 November 2025  Issue Date  25 November 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  20 November 2028  Redemption Date (maturity)  28 November 2028  Barrier  130% of the Initial Reference Price  Barrier End Date  20 November 2028   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nIssue Price\\n\\nProduct Currency\\n\\nNotional Amount (per certificate)\\n\\nBarrier Start Date\\n\\n100%\\n\\nUSD\\n\\nUSD 5,000\\n\\n18 November 2025\\n\\n| ## Underlying  Bloomberg Code  SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust  DIA UP   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a medium term investment horizon (three to five years).\\n- seek to invest in a capital growth product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- seek protection of the Notional Amount at maturity.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n2. If the Final Reference Price is greater than 100% of the Initial Reference Price:\\n- a. If a Barrier Event has occurred: a payment in cash equal to 113% of the Notional Amount\\n- b.  If  a  Barrier  Event  has  not  occurred:  a  payment  in  cash  equal  to  the  Notional Amount increased by the Performance of the Underlying.\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE18416EBF\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE18416EBF-2F8EC-EN.pdf.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 2 out of 7, which is a low risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a low level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nYou are entitled to receive back at least 100% of your capital (capital means Notional Amount). Any amount over this, and any additional return, depends on future market performance and is uncertain. However, this protection against future market performance will not apply if you cash-in before maturity.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  5 years  Example Investment  USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit after 5  years  Minimum  USD 10,000. The return is only guaranteed if you hold the product to maturity.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 9,322  USD 10,000  Average return each year  -6.78%  0.0%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 9,888  USD 10,000  Average return each year  -1.12%  0.0%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,297  USD 11,300  Average return each year  2.97%  4.15%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,356  USD 11,300  Average return each year  3.56%  4.15%   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference asset's past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- In the first year you would get back the amount that you invested (0% annual return). For the other holding periods we have assumed the product performs as shown in the moderate scenario\\n- USD 10,000 is invested.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n| Investment USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit after 5 years  Total costs  USD 308  USD 258  Annual cost impact (*)  3.17%  0.91%   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n(*) This illustrates how costs reduce your return each year over the holding period. For example it shows that if you exit at the recommended holding period your average return per year is projected to be 5.06% before costs and 4.15% after costs.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  2.58% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  USD 258  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  USD 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  USD 0  Transaction costs  0%  USD 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  USD 0   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 28 November 2028, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "9a278774-39c1-4de2-88de-618a90baa5a0", "name": "CE18971EAR-31cd0-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "f1695fd5-c436-4d62-8153-7f3daf18429f", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543701_3cc971e8_CE18971EAR-31cd0-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 3091, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191957938  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  20 November 2025 10:30:39 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying indexes (each index, an Underlying). The product may also pay coupon under predefined conditions in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If the Final Reference Price of the Worst-Performing Underlying is greater than or equal to 60% of its Initial Reference Price: a payment in cash of the Notional Amount.\\n2. If the Final Reference Price of the Worst-Performing Underlying is less than 60% of its Initial Reference Price: a payment in cash equal to 166.67% of the Notional Amount decreased by 166.67% of the Performance of the Worst-Performing Underlying. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  19 November 2025  Issue Date  26 November 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  19 November 2030  Redemption Date (maturity)  26 November 2030  Coupon Valuation Date(s)  See Annex  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  See Annex  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  See Annex  Autocall Barrier(s)  See Annex   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  USD  Notional Amount (per certificate)  USD 1,000   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Coupon Payment Date(s)  See Annex  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  See Annex  Early Redemption Date(s)  See Annex   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  CAC 40 INDEX  CAC  DAX INDEX  DAX  OMXS30 TM  Index  OMX  EURO STOXX® Banks Index  SX7E   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE18971EAR\\n\\nURL: https://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE18971EAR-31cd0-EN.pdf.\\n\\nCoupon: A conditional coupon is due for payment at the relevant Conditional Coupon Rate each time the following condition (Coupon Condition) is met: if, on a Coupon Valuation Date,  the  closing  price  of  each  underlying  is  greater  than  or  equal  to  the  relevant Conditional Coupon Barrier. Otherwise, the coupon is missed but not lost definitely. All missed coupons will accumulate and become payable only if the Coupon Condition is subsequently satisfied.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to the relevant Autocall Barrier, the product will be redeemed  on  the  corresponding  Early  Redemption  Date.  You  will  receive  for  each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a medium term investment horizon (three to five years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 4 out of 7, which is a medium risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 2,381  USD 4,431  (product ends after 26 November  2030)  Average return each year  -76.19%  -15.02%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 9,274  USD 9,340  (product ends after 26 November  2030)  Average return each year  -7.26%  -1.36%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,504  (product ends after 26 August  2026)  Average return  5.04%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,500  USD 11,344  (product ends after 29 November  2027)  Average return each year  5.0%  6.48%   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- USD 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment USD 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 27 May  2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  USD 223  USD 223  Annual cost impact (*)  2.35%  0.46%   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  2.23% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  USD 223  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  USD 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  USD 0  Transaction costs  0%  USD 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  USD 0   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 26 November 2030, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\nThe index sponsor makes no representation whatsoever as to the advisability of purchasing the product and does not sponsor, promote or endorse the product in any manner.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Coupon\\n\\n| Coupon Valuation Date(s)  Coupon Payment Date(s)  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  19 February 2026  26 February 2026  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 May 2026  27 May 2026  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 August 2026  26 August 2026  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 November 2026  27 November 2026  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 February 2027  26 February 2027  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 May 2027  26 May 2027  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 August 2027  26 August 2027  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 November 2027  29 November 2027  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  21 February 2028  28 February 2028  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 May 2028  26 May 2028  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  21 August 2028  28 August 2028  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  20 November 2028  28 November 2028  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 February 2029  26 February 2029  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  21 May 2029  29 May 2029  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  20 August 2029  27 August 2029  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 November 2029  27 November 2029  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 February 2030  26 February 2030  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  20 May 2030  28 May 2030  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 August 2030  26 August 2030  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount  19 November 2030  26 November 2030  65% of the Initial Reference Price  1.68% of the Notional Amount   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## Automatic Early Redemption\\n\\n| Autocall Valuation Date(s)  Early Redemption Date(s)  Autocall Barrier(s)  19 May 2026  27 May 2026  100% of the Initial Reference Price  19 August 2026  26 August 2026  98% of the Initial Reference Price  19 November 2026  27 November 2026  96% of the Initial Reference Price  19 February 2027  26 February 2027  94% of the Initial Reference Price  19 May 2027  26 May 2027  92% of the Initial Reference Price  19 August 2027  26 August 2027  90% of the Initial Reference Price  19 November 2027  29 November 2027  88% of the Initial Reference Price  21 February 2028  28 February 2028  86% of the Initial Reference Price  19 May 2028  26 May 2028  84% of the Initial Reference Price  21 August 2028  28 August 2028  82% of the Initial Reference Price  20 November 2028  28 November 2028  80% of the Initial Reference Price  19 February 2029  26 February 2029  78% of the Initial Reference Price  21 May 2029  29 May 2029  76% of the Initial Reference Price  20 August 2029  27 August 2029  74% of the Initial Reference Price  19 November 2029  27 November 2029  72% of the Initial Reference Price  19 February 2030  26 February 2030  70% of the Initial Reference Price  20 May 2030  28 May 2030  68% of the Initial Reference Price  19 August 2030  26 August 2030  66% of the Initial Reference Price   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## ANNEX"}, {"id": "d4c584f5-abb9-49eb-9098-dc718111429e", "name": "CE19206EAR-DD7FE-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "2e65f4a9-4025-4f69-98e1-b23c470e9978", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543723_59370647_CE19206EAR-DD7FE-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2244, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Certi Plus  ISIN  XS3191931032  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  19 November 2025 00:52:16 CET   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of an underlying index.\\n\\nOn the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate:\\n\\n1. If the Final Reference Price is greater than or equal to 100% of the Initial Reference Price:  a  payment  in  cash  equal  to  the  Notional  Amount  increased  by  160%  of  the Performance of the Underlying.\\n\\n2. If the Final Reference Price is less than 100% of the Initial Reference Price:\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Closing Price of the Underlying observed daily between the Barrier Start Date (excluded) and the Barrier End Date (included) is at least once below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Initial Reference Price is the closing price of the Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price is the closing price of the Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  18 November 2025  Issue Date  25 November 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  18 November 2027  Redemption Date (maturity)  26 November 2027  Barrier  80% of the Initial Reference Price  Barrier End Date  18 November 2027   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## Underlying\\n\\nCSI 300 Index\\n\\nIssue Price\\n\\nProduct Currency\\n\\nNotional Amount (per certificate)\\n\\nBarrier Start Date\\n\\n## Bloomberg Code\\n\\nSHSZ300\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a short term investment horizon (less than three years).\\n- seek to invest in a capital growth product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n- a.  If  a  Barrier  Event  has  not  occurred:  a  payment  in  cash  equal  to  the  Notional Amount.\\n- b. If a Barrier Event has occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount decreased by the Performance of the Underlying. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE19206EAR\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE19206EAR-DD7FE-EN.pdf.\\n\\n100%\\n\\nUSD\\n\\nUSD 1,000\\n\\n18 November 2025\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 4 out of 7, which is a medium risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  5 years  Example Investment  USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit after 5  years  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 2,978  USD 5,050  Average return each year  -70.22%  -28.9%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 7,439  USD 7,055  Average return each year  -25.61%  -15.99%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 9,683  USD 10,000  Average return each year  -3.17%  0.0%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 13,125  USD 15,325  Average return each year  31.25%  23.76%   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference asset's past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- In the first year you would get back the amount that you invested (0% annual return). For the other holding periods we have assumed the product performs as shown in the moderate scenario\\n- USD 10,000 is invested.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n| Investment USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit after 5 years  Total costs  USD 582  USD 532  Annual cost impact (*)  6.14%  2.77%   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n(*) This illustrates how costs reduce your return each year over the holding period. For example it shows that if you exit at the recommended holding period your average return per year is projected to be 2.77% before costs and 0.0% after costs.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  5.32% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  USD 532  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  USD 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  USD 0  Transaction costs  0%  USD 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  USD 0   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 26 November 2027, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\nThe index sponsor makes no representation whatsoever as to the advisability of purchasing the product and does not sponsor, promote or endorse the product in any manner.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "3e580e5e-8076-4cdf-acc0-876e5e2a9710", "name": "CE19983EBF-15CA4-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "68ef5fca-8200-4ee3-92b2-fdc5b67c7801", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543724_6f037f53_CE19983EBF-15CA4-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 3005, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191958076  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  21 November 2025 00:42:17 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying shares (each share, an Underlying). The product may also pay coupon under predefined conditions in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If a Barrier Event has not occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount.\\n2.  If  a  Barrier  Event  has  occurred:  delivery  of  the  number  of  shares  of  the  WorstPerforming Underlying (as determined below) plus a payment in cash in respect of any fraction of a share. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price of at least one Underlying is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n\\nThe Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n- The number of shares of an underlying is the Notional Amount per certificate divided by its Initial Reference Price converted, if necessary, into the Product Currency using the applicable exchange rate on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  20 November 2025  Issue Date  28 November 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  20 November 2030  Redemption Date (maturity)  27 November 2030  Coupon Valuation Date(s)  See Annex  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  See Annex  Barrier  60% of the Initial Reference Price  Early Redemption Date(s)  See Annex   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  USD  Notional Amount (per certificate)  USD 10,000   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Coupon Payment Date(s)  See Annex  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  See Annex  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  See Annex   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  ISIN  Hong Kong Exchanges &amp; Clearing Ltd  388 HK  HK0388045442  China Construction Bank Corp  939 HK  CNE1000002H1   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE19983EBF\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE19983EBF-15CA4-EN.pdf.\\n\\nCoupon: A conditional coupon is due for payment at the relevant Conditional Coupon Rate each time the following condition (Coupon Condition) is met: if, on a Coupon Valuation Date,  the  closing  price  of  each  underlying  is  greater  than  or  equal  to  the  relevant Conditional Coupon Barrier. Otherwise, the coupon is missed but not lost definitely. All missed coupons will accumulate and become payable only if the Coupon Condition is subsequently satisfied.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to 100% of its Initial Reference Price, the product will be redeemed on the corresponding Early Redemption Date. You will receive for each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a medium term investment horizon (three to five years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 6 out of 7, which is the second-highest risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a high level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 859  USD 1,022  (product ends after 27 November  2030)  Average return each year  -91.41%  -36.64%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 5,950  USD 3,230  (product ends after 27 November  2030)  Average return each year  -40.5%  -20.24%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,630  (product ends after 27 February  2026)  Average return  6.3%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 11,874  USD 15,670  (product ends after 28 February  2028)  Average return each year  18.74%  22.07%   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- USD 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment USD 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 27 February  2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  USD 153  USD 153  Annual cost impact (*)  1.65%  0.31%   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  1.53% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  USD 153  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  USD 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  USD 0  Transaction costs  0%  USD 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  USD 0   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 27 November 2030, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation wi