ives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nthe amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- GBP 10,000 is invested\\n\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment GBP 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 30  December 2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  GBP 361  GBP 361  Annual cost impact (*)  3.92%  0.63%   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n(*) This illustrates how costs reduce your return each year over the holding period. For example it shows that if you exit at maturity your average return per year is projected to be 1.8% before costs and 1.17% after costs.\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  3.61% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  GBP 361  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  GBP 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of your investment per year.  GBP 0  Transaction costs  0%  GBP 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  GBP 0   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 30 December 2031, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\nThe index sponsor makes no representation whatsoever as to the advisability of purchasing the product and does not sponsor, promote or endorse the product in any manner.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Coupon\\n\\n| Coupon Valuation Date(s)  Coupon Payment Date(s)  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  22 June 2026  29 June 2026  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  21 December 2026  30 December 2026  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  21 June 2027  28 June 2027  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  20 December 2027  29 December 2027  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  20 June 2028  27 June 2028  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  19 December 2028  28 December 2028  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  20 June 2029  27 June 2029  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  19 December 2029  28 December 2029  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  20 June 2030  27 June 2030  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  19 December 2030  30 December 2030  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  20 June 2031  27 June 2031  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount  19 December 2031  30 December 2031  85% of the Initial Reference Price  4.61% of the Notional Amount   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## ANNEX"}, {"id": "be80564c-8bbf-4280-888f-903a8b80f4e4", "name": "CE27878YFR-A9EC5-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "da8ea64d-feaf-4a08-ab61-058eff20d854", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543757_522eacb4_CE27878YFR-A9EC5-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2476, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191970956  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  21 November 2025 00:39:08 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n- OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying indexes (each index, an Underlying).\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply.\\n\\nOn the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate:\\n\\n1.  If  in  respect  of  each  underlying  in  the  Basket,  the  official  closing  price  of  such underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date or any of the Automatic Early Redemption Valuation Date is greater than or equal to 100% of its Initial Reference Price: a payment in cash equal to 170.5% of the Notional Amount.\\n2. If the Final Reference Price of the Worst-Performing Underlying is less than 100% of its Initial Reference Price:\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price of at least one Underlying is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  19 December 2025  Issue Price  100%  Issue Date  30 December 2025  Product Currency  GBP  Redemption Valuation Date  19 December 2031  Notional Amount (per certificate)  GBP 1,000  Redemption Date (maturity)  30 December 2031  Barrier  70% of the Initial Reference Price  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  21 December 2026, 21 June 2027, 20  December 2027, 20 June 2028, 19  December 2028, 20 June 2029, 19  December 2029, 20 June 2030, 19  December 2030 and 20 June 2031  Early Redemption Date(s)  30 December 2026, 28 June 2027, 29  December 2027, 27 June 2028, 28  December 2028, 27 June 2029, 28  December 2029, 27 June 2030, 30  December 2030 and 27 June 2031  Exit Rate(s)  11.75%, 17.6250%, 23.50%, 29.3750%,  35.25%, 41.1250%, 47%, 52.8750%, 58.75%  and 64.6250% of the Notional Amount   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  FTSE MIB INDEX  FTSEMIB  NASDAQ 100® Index  NDX  NIKKEI 225  NKY   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE27878YFR\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE27878YFR-A9EC5-EN.pdf.\\n\\n- a.  If  a  Barrier  Event  has  not  occurred:  a  payment  in  cash  equal  to  the  Notional Amount.\\n- b. If a Barrier Event has occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount decreased by the Performance of the Worst-Performing Underlying. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\nAutomatic  Early  Redemption:  If,  on  any  Autocall  Valuation  Date,  in  respect  of  each underlying, the closing price of such underlying on that Autocall Valuation Date or any of the Autocall Valuation Date which precede that Autocall Valuation Date is greater than or equal  to  100%  of  its  Initial  Reference  Price,  the  product  will  be  redeemed  on  the corresponding Early Redemption Date. You will receive for each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount plus a premium based on the relevant Exit Rate\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a long term investment horizon (over five years).\\n- seek to invest in a capital growth product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 5 out of 7, which is a medium-high risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium-high level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  GBP 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  GBP 1,423  GBP 1,431  (product ends after 30 December  2031)  Average return each year  -85.77%  -27.68%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  GBP 6,502  GBP 3,691  (product ends after 30 December  2031)  Average return each year  -34.98%  -15.31%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  GBP 11,175  (product ends after 30 December  2026)  Average return each year  11.75%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  GBP 10,496  GBP 14,113  (product ends after 27 June 2029)  Average return each year  4.96%  10.37%   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- GBP 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment GBP 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 30  December 2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  GBP 708  GBP 708  Annual cost impact (*)  8.51%  1.25%   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  7.08% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  GBP 708  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  GBP 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  GBP 0  Transaction costs  0%  GBP 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  GBP 0   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 30 December 2031, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\nThe index sponsor makes no representation whatsoever as to the advisability of purchasing the product and does not sponsor, promote or endorse the product in any manner.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "38301d0b-cce0-43b4-b8ed-925a993b8c32", "name": "CE33556MLS-1D062-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "754b3cfb-2aed-4964-9cd2-0b255e58eedf", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543782_c6a92f69_CE33556MLS-1D062-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2525, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191943474  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  19 November 2025 01:03:31 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying  shares  (each  share,  an  Underlying).  The  product  will  also  pay  coupon  in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If a Barrier Event has not occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price of at least one Underlying is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n- The number of shares of an underlying is the Notional Amount per certificate divided by its Initial Reference Price converted, if necessary, into the Product Currency using the applicable exchange rate on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  18 November 2025  Issue Date  25 November 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  25 May 2028  Redemption Date (maturity)  02 June 2028  Coupon Payment Date(s)  25 February 2026, 26 May 2026, 25 August  2026, 25 November 2026, 25 February 2027,  25 May 2027, 25 August 2027, 26 November  2027, 28 February 2028 and 02 June 2028  Barrier  70% of the Initial Reference Price  Early Redemption Date(s)  26 May 2026, 25 August 2026, 25 November  2026, 25 February 2027, 25 May 2027, 25  August 2027, 26 November 2027 and 28  February 2028   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  USD  Notional Amount (per certificate)  USD 1,000   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Coupon Rate(s)  2.8750% of the Notional Amount  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  18 May 2026, 18 August 2026, 18 November  2026, 18 February 2027, 18 May 2027, 18  August 2027, 18 November 2027 and 18  February 2028   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE33556MLS URL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE33556MLS-1D062-EN.pdf.\\n\\n2.  If  a  Barrier  Event  has  occurred:  delivery  of  the  number  of  shares  of  the  WorstPerforming Underlying (as determined below) plus a payment in cash in respect of any fraction of a share. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\nCoupon: A coupon is due for payment at the Coupon Rate on each Coupon Payment Date.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to 95% of its Initial Reference Price, the product will be redeemed on the corresponding Early Redemption Date. You will receive for each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  ISIN  Cisco Systems Inc  CSCO UW  US17275R1023  Kering SA  KER FP  FR0000121485  Shell PLC  SHELL NA  GB00BP6MXD84   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a short term investment horizon (less than three years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 4 out of 7, which is a medium risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  USD 2,875. The return is only guaranteed if you hold the product to maturity.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 4,244  USD 4,971  (product ends after 02 June 2028)  Average return each year  -57.56%  -24.24%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 7,988  USD 6,897  (product ends after 02 June 2028)  Average return each year  -20.12%  -13.72%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,575  (product ends after 26 May 2026)  Average return  5.75%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,845  USD 12,300  (product ends after 26 November  2027)  Average return each year  8.45%  10.89%   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- USD 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment USD 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 26 May  2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  USD 550  USD 550  Annual cost impact (*)  6.15%  2.32%   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  5.5% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  USD 550  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  USD 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  USD 0  Transaction costs  0%  USD 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  USD 0   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 02 June 2028, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "fe05a8a1-0705-41e1-b5b7-4967922ae0e3", "name": "CE33598MLS-5708C-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "f7f0da28-2d73-41fb-b92b-67ff34707f31", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543784_5b4f87ff_CE33598MLS-5708C-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2809, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191978009  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  25 February 2026 08:55:59 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying indexes (each index, an Underlying). The product may also pay coupon under predefined conditions in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If a Barrier Event has not occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount.\\n2. If a Barrier Event has occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount decreased by the Performance of the Worst-Performing Underlying. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price of at least one Underlying is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n\\nThe Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is as specified in the table of Underlying below.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  21 November 2025  Issue Date  27 November 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  20 November 2029  Redemption Date (maturity)  27 November 2029  Coupon Valuation Date(s)  See Annex  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  See Annex  Barrier  55% of the Initial Reference Price  Early Redemption Date(s)  See Annex   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  CHF  Notional Amount (per certificate)  CHF 1,000   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Coupon Payment Date(s)  See Annex  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  See Annex  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  See Annex   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  Initial Reference Price  Strike Date  NIKKEI 225  NKY  21 November 2025  NASDAQ 100® Index  NDX  20 November 2025  OMXS30 TM  Index  OMX  20 November 2025  EURO STOXX 50®  SX5E  20 November 2025   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE33598MLS\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE33598MLS-5708C-EN.pdf.\\n\\nCoupon: A conditional coupon is due for payment at the relevant Conditional Coupon Rate each time the following condition (Coupon Condition) is met: if, on a Coupon Valuation Date,  the  closing  price  of  each  underlying  is  greater  than  or  equal  to  the  relevant Conditional Coupon Barrier. Otherwise, the coupon is missed but not lost definitely. All missed coupons will accumulate and become payable only if the Coupon Condition is subsequently satisfied.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to 93% of its Initial Reference Price, the product will be redeemed on the corresponding Early Redemption Date. You will receive for each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a medium term investment horizon (three to five years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 1 out of 7, which is the lowest risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a very low level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  CHF 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  CHF 9,960  (product ends after 03 March  2026)  Average return  -0.4%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  CHF 9,960  (product ends after 03 March  2026)  Average return  -0.4%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  CHF 9,960  (product ends after 03 March  2026)  Average return  -0.4%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  CHF 9,960  (product ends after 03 March  2026)  Average return  -0.4%   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- CHF 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment CHF 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 03 March  2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  CHF 33  CHF 33  Annual cost impact (*)  0.33%  0.09%   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  0.33% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  CHF 33  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  CHF 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of your investment per year.  CHF 0  Transaction costs  0%  CHF 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  CHF 0   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 27 November 2029, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\nThe index sponsor makes no representation whatsoever as to the advisability of purchasing the product and does not sponsor, promote or endorse the product in any manner.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Coupon\\n\\n| Coupon Valuation Date(s)  Coupon Payment Date(s)  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  24 February 2026  03 March 2026  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  21 May 2026  28 May 2026  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  21 August 2026  28 August 2026  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  24 November 2026  01 December 2026  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  22 February 2027  01 March 2027  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  21 May 2027  28 May 2027  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  23 August 2027  30 August 2027  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  22 November 2027  29 November 2027  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  22 February 2028  29 February 2028  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  22 May 2028  29 May 2028  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  21 August 2028  28 August 2028  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  21 November 2028  28 November 2028  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  21 February 2029  28 February 2029  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  21 May 2029  28 May 2029  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  21 August 2029  28 August 2029  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount  20 November 2029  27 November 2029  80% of the Initial Reference Price  1.72% of the Notional Amount   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## Automatic Early Redemption\\n\\n| Autocall Valuation Date(s)  Early Redemption Date(s)  24 February 2026  03 March 2026  21 May 2026  28 May 2026  21 August 2026  28 August 2026  24 November 2026  01 December 2026  22 February 2027  01 March 2027  21 May 2027  28 May 2027  23 August 2027  30 August 2027  22 November 2027  29 November 2027  22 February 2028  29 February 2028  22 May 2028  29 May 2028  21 August 2028  28 August 2028  21 November 2028  28 November 2028  21 February 2029  28 February 2029  21 May 2029  28 May 2029  21 August 2029  28 August 2029   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## ANNEX"}, {"id": "2cc7f8d7-dd09-45be-abba-ecf6af89cd3b", "name": "CE35292YAF-B79CD-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "22d11b8a-4584-4895-9d3b-cad018e40950", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543767_ff07087a_CE35292YAF-B79CD-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2476, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3152091701  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  21 November 2025 00:19:11 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying indexes (each index, an Underlying). The product may also pay coupon under predefined conditions in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If a Barrier Event has not occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount.\\n2. If a Barrier Event has occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount decreased by the Performance of the Worst-Performing Underlying. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price of at least one Underlying is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n\\nThe Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  21 November 2025  Issue Date  28 November 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  21 November 2031  Redemption Date (maturity)  28 November 2031  Coupon Valuation Date(s)  23 November 2026, 22 November 2027, 21  November 2028, 21 November 2029, 21  November 2030 and 21 November 2031  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  85% of the Initial Reference Price  Barrier  65% of the Initial Reference Price  Early Redemption Date(s)  28 November 2028, 28 November 2029 and  29 November 2030   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  USD  Notional Amount (per certificate)  USD 1,000   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Coupon Payment Date(s)  30 November 2026, 29 November 2027, 28  November 2028, 28 November 2029, 29  November 2030 and 28 November 2031  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  8% of the Notional Amount  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  21 November 2028, 21 November 2029 and  21 November 2030   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  S&amp;P 500® Index  SPX  EURO STOXX 50®  SX5E  HANG SENG INDEX  HSI   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE35292YAF\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE35292YAF-B79CD-EN.pdf.\\n\\nCoupon: A conditional coupon is due for payment at the relevant Conditional Coupon Rate each time the following condition (Coupon Condition) is met: if, on a Coupon Valuation Date,  the  closing  price  of  each  underlying  is  greater  than  or  equal  to  the  relevant Conditional Coupon Barrier. Otherwise, the coupon is missed but not lost definitely. All missed coupons will accumulate and become payable only if the Coupon Condition is subsequently satisfied.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to 100% of its Initial Reference Price, the product will be redeemed on the corresponding Early Redemption Date. You will receive for each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a long term investment horizon (over five years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 5 out of 7, which is a medium-high risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium-high level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 1,707  USD 1,725  (product ends after 28 November  2031)  Average return each year  -82.93%  -25.39%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 7,088  USD 3,963  (product ends after 28 November  2031)  Average return each year  -29.12%  -14.3%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 9,673  USD 12,400  (product ends after 28 November  2028)  Average return each year  -3.27%  7.43%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 10,872  USD 14,000  (product ends after 29 November  2030)  Average return each year  8.72%  6.96%   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- USD 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment USD 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 28  November 2028  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  USD 940  USD 940  Annual cost impact (*)  3.6%  1.72%   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  9.4% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  USD 940  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  USD 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  USD 0  Transaction costs  0%  USD 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  USD 0   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 28 November 2031, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\nThe index sponsor makes no representation whatsoever as to the advisability of purchasing the product and does not sponsor, promote or endorse the product in any manner.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "7865af1a-8625-46c3-9a49-4a6bf6249344", "name": "CE39215DRE-DCB5C-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "12b7aab5-c525-4d10-bfef-45761087f0e9", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543773_6a4fe81b_CE39215DRE-DCB5C-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2868, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191959553  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  28 February 2026 02:38:28 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n- OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThis certificate provides a return which depends on the performance over the lifetime of the  certificate  of  an  underlying  redeemable  preference  share  issued  by  BNP  Paribas Synergy Limited the value of which is in turn linked to the performance of an underlying share and/or index or basket of shares and/or indices. The description below is therefore based on the expected value of such preference share however the real return will depend on the actual value of the preference share.\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying indexes (each index, an Underlying). The product may also pay coupon under predefined conditions in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply.\\n\\nOn the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate:\\n\\n1. If a Barrier Event has not occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price of at least one Underlying is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  19 November 2025  Issue Date  03 December 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  19 November 2029  Redemption Date (maturity)  03 December 2029  Coupon Valuation Date(s)  See Annex  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  See Annex  Barrier  65% of the Initial Reference Price  Early Redemption Date(s)  See Annex   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nIssue Price\\n\\nProduct Currency\\n\\nNotional Amount (per certificate)\\n\\nConditional Coupon Barrier(s)\\n\\nAutocall Valuation Date(s)\\n\\nAutocall Barrier(s)\\n\\n100%\\n\\nGBP\\n\\nGBP 1,000\\n\\nSee Annex\\n\\nSee Annex\\n\\nSee Annex\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  STOXX® 600 Bank  SX7P  STOXX® Europe 600 Basic Resources  SXPP  STOXX® 600 Utilities  SX6P   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThese events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\n2. If a Barrier Event has occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount decreased by the Performance of the Worst-Performing Underlying. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\nCoupon: A conditional coupon is due for payment at the relevant Conditional Coupon Rate each time the following condition (Coupon Condition) is met: if, on a Coupon Valuation Date,  the  closing  price  of  each  underlying  is  greater  than  or  equal  to  the  relevant Conditional Coupon Barrier. Otherwise, the coupon is missed but not lost definitely. All missed coupons will accumulate and become payable only if the Coupon Condition is subsequently satisfied.\\n\\nAll due conditional coupons will be paid at the Redemption Date or upon early redemption.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to the relevant Autocall Barrier, the product will be redeemed  on  the  corresponding  Early  Redemption  Date.  You  will  receive  for  each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE39215DRE\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE39215DRE-DCB5C-EN.pdf.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a medium term investment horizon (three to five years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 4 out of 7, which is a medium risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  GBP 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  GBP 3,078  GBP 4,864  (product ends after 03 December  2029)  Average return each year  -69.22%  -17.42%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  GBP 10,655  (product ends after 03 December  2026)  Average return  6.55%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  GBP 10,655  (product ends after 03 December  2026)  Average return  6.55%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  GBP 10,655  (product ends after 03 December  2026)  Average return  6.55%   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- GBP 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment GBP 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 03  December 2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  GBP 0  GBP 0  Annual cost impact (*)  0.0%  0.0%   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  0% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  GBP 0  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  GBP 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of your investment per year.  GBP 0  Transaction costs  0%  GBP 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  GBP 0   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 03 December 2029, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\nThe index sponsor makes no representation whatsoever as to the advisability of purchasing the product and does not sponsor, promote or endorse the product in any manner.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Coupon\\n\\n| Coupon Valuation Date(s)  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  19 February 2026  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 May 2026  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 August 2026  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 November 2026  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 February 2027  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 May 2027  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 August 2027  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 November 2027  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  21 February 2028  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 May 2028  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  21 August 2028  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  20 November 2028  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 February 2029  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  21 May 2029  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  20 August 2029  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount  19 November 2029  75% of the Initial Reference Price  3.28% of the Notional Amount   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## Automatic Early Redemption\\n\\n| Autocall Valuation Date(s)  Early Redemption Date(s)  Autocall Barrier(s)  19 November 2026  03 December 2026  95% of the Initial Reference Price  19 February 2027  05 March 2027  90% of the Initial Reference Price  19 May 2027  02 June 2027  90% of the Initial Reference Price  19 August 2027  02 September 2027  90% of the Initial Reference Price  19 November 2027  03 December 2027  90% of the Initial Reference Price  21 February 2028  06 March 2028  85% of the Initial Reference Price  19 May 2028  02 June 2028  85% of the Initial Reference Price  21 August 2028  04 September 2028  80% of the Initial Reference Price  20 November 2028  04 December 2028  80% of the Initial Reference Price  19 February 2029  05 March 2029  75% of the Initial Reference Price  21 May 2029  04 June 2029  75% of the Initial Reference Price  20 August 2029  03 September 2029  75% of the Initial Reference Price   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## ANNEX"}, {"id": "39154fb1-b0ee-4916-9a32-d915d5a0dceb", "name": "CE39280DRE-42DD1-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "1e1ab853-8811-46dc-86b3-3e0e6c95a115", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543776_04513e46_CE39280DRE-42DD1-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2627, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191979312  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  24 February 2026 07:26:46 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of a basket (the Basket) composed of underlying shares (each share, an Underlying). The product may also pay coupon under predefined conditions in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If a Barrier Event has not occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount.\\n2. If a Barrier Event has occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount decreased by the Performance of the Basket. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Value of the Basket is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of the Basket is the difference between the Final Value of the Basket and 100%, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Final Value of the Basket is the average of the Final Reference Values of all the Underlyings.\\n- The Final Reference Value of an Underlying is its Final Reference Price divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Reference Value:\\n- for the Basket, on a given date, is the average of the Reference Values of all the Underlyings on such date.\\n- for an Underlying, on a given date, is its closing price on such date divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  21 November 2025  Issue Date  01 December 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  22 November 2027  Redemption Date (maturity)  01 December 2027  Coupon Valuation Date(s)  23 February 2026, 21 May 2026, 21 August  2026, 23 November 2026, 22 February 2027,  21 May 2027, 23 August 2027 and 22  November 2027  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  93%  Barrier  93%  Early Redemption Date(s)  04 March 2026, 01 June 2026, 31 August  2026, 02 December 2026, 03 March 2027,  31 May 2027 and 01 September 2027   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  EUR  Notional Amount (per certificate)  EUR 1,000   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Coupon Payment Date(s)  04 March 2026, 01 June 2026, 31 August  2026, 02 December 2026, 03 March 2027,  31 May 2027, 01 September 2027 and 01  December 2027  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  1.8125% of the Notional Amount  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  23 February 2026, 21 May 2026, 21 August  2026, 23 November 2026, 22 February 2027,  21 May 2027 and 23 August 2027   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  ISIN  See Annex  See Annex  See Annex   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE39280DRE\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE39280DRE-42DD1-EN.pdf.\\n\\nCoupon: A conditional coupon is due for payment at the relevant Conditional Coupon Rate each time the following condition (Coupon Condition) is met: if, on a Coupon Valuation Date,  the  Reference  Value  of  the  Basket  is  greater  than  or  equal  to  the  relevant Conditional Coupon Barrier. Otherwise, the coupon is missed but not lost definitely. All missed coupons will accumulate and become payable only if the Coupon Condition is subsequently satisfied.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the Reference Value of the  Basket  is  greater  than  or  equal  to  99%,  the  product  will  be  redeemed  on  the corresponding Early Redemption Date. You will receive for each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\nThe product terms provide that if certain exceptional events occur (1) adjustments may be made to the product and/or (2) the Issuer of the product may terminate the product early. These events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a short term investment horizon (less than three years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 1 out of 7, which is the lowest risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a very low level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  EUR 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 9,800  (product ends after 04 March  2026)  Average return  -2.0%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 9,800  (product ends after 04 March  2026)  Average return  -2.0%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 9,800  (product ends after 04 March  2026)  Average return  -2.0%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 9,800  (product ends after 04 March  2026)  Average return  -2.0%   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- EUR 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment EUR 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 04 March  2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  EUR 209  EUR 209  Annual cost impact (*)  2.02%  1.14%   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  2.09% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  EUR 209  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  EUR 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of your investment per year.  EUR 0  Transaction costs  0%  EUR 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  EUR 0   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 01 December 2027, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Underlyings\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  ISIN  Bristol-Myers Squibb Co  BMY UN  US1101221083  Pfizer Inc  PFE UN  US7170811035  Sanofi SA  SAN FP  FR0000120578  Novo Nordisk A/S  NOVOB DC  DK0062498333  Bayer AG  BAYN GY  DE000BAY0017  Merck KGaA  MRK GY  DE0006599905   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## ANNEX"}, {"id": "76e3328c-97ef-4070-b828-1aba3ac8c1f5", "name": "CE43256EAG-E38C0-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "b1dbb69a-9c97-4aca-b232-454f30f42c57", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543797_1e7b8baa_CE43256EAG-E38C0-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2609, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| ## PHOENIX PLUS STEP DOWN (SECURITY)  ISIN  XS3191963829  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  28 February 2026 11:03:51 CET   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying shares (each share, an Underlying). The product may also pay coupon under predefined conditions in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If the Final Reference Price of the Worst-Performing Underlying is greater than or equal to 55% of its Initial Reference Price: a payment in cash of the Notional Amount.\\n2. If the Final Reference Price of the Worst-Performing Underlying is less than 55% of its  Initial  Reference  Price:  delivery  of  the  number  of  shares  of  the  Worst-Performing Underlying (as determined below) plus a payment in cash in respect of any fraction of a share. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n- The number of shares of an underlying is the Notional Amount per certificate divided by 55% of its Initial Reference Price converted, if necessary, into the Product Currency using the applicable exchange rate on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  19 November 2025  Issue Date  03 December 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  19 November 2029  Redemption Date (maturity)  03 December 2029  Coupon Valuation Date(s)  19 May 2026, 19 November 2026, 19 May  2027, 19 November 2027, 19 May 2028, 20  November 2028, 21 May 2029 and 19  November 2029  Conditional Coupon Barrier(s)  55% of the Initial Reference Price  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  19 November 2026, 19 May 2027, 19  November 2027, 19 May 2028, 20 November  2028 and 21 May 2029  Autocall Barrier(s)  95%, 90%, 85%, 80%, 75% and 70% of the  Initial Reference Price   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nCoupon: A conditional coupon is due for payment at the relevant Conditional Coupon Rate each time the following condition (Coupon Condition) is met: if, on a Coupon Valuation Date,  the  closing  price  of  each  underlying  is  greater  than  or  equal  to  the  relevant Conditional Coupon Barrier. Otherwise, the coupon is missed but not lost definitely. All missed coupons will accumulate and become payable only if the Coupon Condition is subsequently satisfied.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to the relevant Autocall Barrier, the product will be redeemed  on  the  corresponding  Early  Redemption  Date.  You  will  receive  for  each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\nIssue Price\\n\\nProduct Currency\\n\\nNotional Amount (per certificate)\\n\\n100%\\n\\nEUR\\n\\nEUR 1,000\\n\\n| Coupon Payment Date(s)  02 June 2026, 03 December 2026, 02 June  2027, 03 December 2027, 02 June 2028, 04  December 2028, 04 June 2029 and 03  December 2029  Conditional Coupon Rate(s)  5% of the Notional Amount  Early Redemption Date(s)  03 December 2026, 02 June 2027, 03  December 2027, 02 June 2028, 04  December 2028 and 04 June 2029   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE43256EAG\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE43256EAG-E38C0-EN.pdf.\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  ISIN  TotalEnergies SE  TTE FP  FR0000120271  Compagnie de Saint-Gobain  SGO FP  FR0000125007  Safran SA  SAF FP  FR0000073272  Baidu Inc  BIDU UW  US0567521085   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThese events are specified in the product terms and principally relate to the Underlying(s), the product and the Issuer of the product. The return (if any) you receive on such early termination is likely to be different from the scenarios described above and may be less than the amount you invested.\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a medium term investment horizon (three to five years).\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nLower Risk\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nHigher Risk\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 5 out of 7, which is a medium-high risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium-high level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted. The scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  EUR 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  There is no minimum guaranteed return. You could lose some or all of your Investment.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 598  EUR 1,211  (product ends after 03 December  2029)  Average return each year  -94.02%  -42.93%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 7,703  EUR 5,058  (product ends after 03 December  2029)  Average return each year  -22.97%  -16.56%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 10,825  (product ends after 03 December  2026)  Average return  8.25%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 10,834  EUR 12,793  (product ends after 04 December  2028)  Average return each year  8.34%  9.31%   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nthe amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- EUR 10,000 is invested\\n\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment EUR 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 03  December 2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  EUR 0  EUR 0  Annual cost impact (*)  0.0%  0.0%   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  0% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  EUR 0  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  EUR 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of your investment per year.  EUR 0  Transaction costs  0%  EUR 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  EUR 0   |\\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 03 December 2029, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "24d7381a-1bae-4c99-9b39-93aa9c9eaca5", "name": "CE47039JAV-BF29C-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "201c18fc-a587-430f-ad45-f1ced9dea77b", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543788_14217a99_CE47039JAV-BF29C-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2331, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191949166  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  19 November 2025 00:35:41 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has a full capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n- OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying shares (each share, an Underlying).\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply.\\n\\nOn the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate:\\n\\n1. If the Final Reference Price of the Worst-Performing Underlying is greater than or equal to 100% of its Initial  Reference Price:  a  payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount plus a premium being the maximum between the Performance of the WorstPerforming Underlying and 30.5%.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- The Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Strike Date.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  18 November 2025  Issue Date  02 December 2025  Redemption Date (maturity)  02 December 2030  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  18 May 2026, 18 November 2026, 18 May  2027, 18 November 2027, 18 May 2028, 20  November 2028, 18 May 2029, 19 November  2029 and 20 May 2030  Exit Rate(s)  3.05%, 6.10%, 9.15%, 12.20%, 15.25%,  18.30%, 21.35%, 24.40% and 27.45% of the  Notional Amount   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  EUR  Notional Amount (per certificate)  EUR 1,000  Early Redemption Date(s)  01 June 2026, 02 December 2026, 01 June  2027, 02 December 2027, 01 June 2028, 04  December 2028, 01 June 2029, 03  December 2029 and 03 June 2030   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  ISIN  Amazon.com Inc  AMZN UW  US0231351067  NextEra Energy Inc  NEE UN  US65339F1012  Leidos Holdings Inc  LDOS UN  US5253271028  Meta Platforms Inc  META UW  US30303M1027   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\n## This product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a medium term investment horizon (three to five years).\\n- seek to invest in a capital growth product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n2. If the Final Reference Price of the Worst-Performing Underlying is less than 100% of its Initial Reference Price: a payment in cash equal to 100% of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE47039JAV\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE47039JAV-BF29C-EN.pdf.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to 100% of its Initial Reference Price, the product will be redeemed on the corresponding Early Redemption Date. You will receive for each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount plus a premium based on the relevant Exit Rate\\n\\n- seek protection of the Notional Amount at maturity and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 2 out of 7, which is a low risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a low level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nYou are entitled to receive back at least 100% of your capital (capital means Notional Amount). Any amount over this, and any additional return, depends on future market performance and is uncertain. However, this protection against future market performance will not apply if you cash-in before maturity.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  EUR 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  EUR 10,000. The return is only guaranteed if you hold the product to maturity.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 8,726  EUR 10,000  (product ends after 02 December  2030)  Average return each year  -12.74%  0.0%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 8,998  EUR 10,000  (product ends after 02 December  2030)  Average return each year  -10.02%  0.0%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 10,305  (product ends after 01 June 2026)  Average return  3.05%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  EUR 10,382  EUR 12,135  (product ends after 01 June 2029)  Average return each year  3.82%  5.69%   |\\n|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n- EUR 10,000 is invested\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment EUR 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 01 June  2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  EUR 357  EUR 357  Annual cost impact (*)  3.82%  0.73%   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nFor the first call date being less than one year the result is not annualized.\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  3.57% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  EUR 357  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  EUR 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  EUR 0  Transaction costs  0%  EUR 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  EUR 0   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 02 December 2030, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\n<!-- image -->"}, {"id": "9765ea1b-a1ca-42fc-9650-e7c3be6be830", "name": "CE47050JAV-F4B7A-EN.pdf", "type": "file", "fileId": "14de1c77-5c96-473c-a9d1-eb47da56274a", "status": "parsed", "fileKey": "6ec24660-eb86-4118-8548-194f6a707b7e/1772561543791_0949236c_CE47050JAV-F4B7A-EN.pdf", "tokenCount": 2684, "parsedContent": "<!-- image -->\\n\\n## KEY INFORMATION DOCUMENT\\n\\n## PURPOSE\\n\\nThis document provides you with key information about this investment product. It is not marketing material. The information is required by law to help you understand the nature, risks, costs, potential gains and losses of this product and to help you compare it with other products.\\n\\n## PRODUCT\\n\\n| Autocall  ISIN  XS3191949240  Manufacturer  BNP Paribas S.A.  - www.bnpparibas.com - Call +33 (0)1 57 08 22 00 for more information  Issuer:  BNP Paribas Issuance B.V. -  Guarantor:  BNP Paribas S.A.  Competent Authority  Autorité des marchés financiers (AMF) is responsible for supervising BNP Paribas S.A. in relation to this Key Information Document  KID Production Date  20 November 2025 10:37:56 CET   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nYou are about to purchase a product that is not simple and may be difficult to understand.\\n\\n## WHAT IS THIS PRODUCT?\\n\\n## TYPE\\n\\nThis product is a certificate, a transferable debt instrument. It has no capital protection against market risk at maturity.\\n\\n## TERM\\n\\nThis product has a fixed term and will redeem on the Redemption Date unless redeemed early in accordance with the Automatic Early Redemption provisions below.\\n\\n## OBJECTIVES\\n\\nThe objective of this product is to provide you with a return based on the performance of underlying  shares  (each  share,  an  Underlying).  The  product  will  also  pay  coupon  in accordance with the Coupon provisions below.\\n\\nUnless the product has been redeemed early, the following provisions would apply. On the Redemption Date you will receive in respect of each certificate, in addition to any final payment of a coupon:\\n\\n1. If a Barrier Event has not occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount.\\n\\n## Where:\\n\\n- A Barrier Event shall be deemed to occur if the Final Reference Price of at least one Underlying is below the Barrier.\\n- The Performance of an Underlying is the difference between its Final Reference Price and its Initial Reference Price, divided by its Initial Reference Price, expressed in absolute value.\\n- The Worst-Performing Underlying is the Underlying that shows the lowest Final Reference Price when divided by its Initial Reference Price.\\n- The Initial Reference Price of an Underlying is as specified in the table of Underlying below.\\n- The Final Reference Price of an Underlying is the closing price of that Underlying on the Redemption Valuation Date.\\n\\n## PRODUCT DATA\\n\\n| Strike Date  19 November 2025  Issue Date  04 December 2025  Redemption Valuation Date  29 November 2027  Redemption Date (maturity)  13 December 2027  Coupon Payment Date(s)  See Annex  Barrier  60% of the Initial Reference Price  Early Redemption Date(s)  See Annex   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Issue Price  100%  Product Currency  USD  Notional Amount (per certificate)  USD 1,000   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Coupon Rate(s)  See Annex  Autocall Valuation Date(s)  See Annex  Autocall Barrier(s)  See Annex   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n| Underlying  Bloomberg Code  ISIN  Initial Reference Price  Strike Date  Alphabet Inc  GOOGL UW  US02079K3059  18 November 2025  VanEck Semiconductor ETF  SMH UQ  US92189F6768  18 November 2025  Nordea Bank Abp  NDA SS  FI4000297767  19 November 2025   |\\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nAll redemptions described in this document (including potential gains) are calculated on the basis of the Notional Amount, excluding costs, social contributions and taxation applicable to this type of investment.\\n\\n## INTENDED RETAIL INVESTOR\\n\\nThis product has been designed for retail investors who:\\n\\n- have a short term investment horizon (less than three years).\\n2. If a Barrier Event has occurred: a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount decreased by the Performance of the Worst-Performing Underlying. In this case you will suffer a partial or total loss of the Notional Amount.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nInternal Ref.: CE47050JAV\\n\\nURL: http://kid.bnpparibas.com/CE47050JAV-F4B7A-EN.pdf.\\n\\nCoupon: A coupon is due for payment at the Coupon Rate on each Coupon Payment Date.\\n\\nAutomatic Early Redemption: If, on any Autocall Valuation Date, the closing price of each underlying is greater than or equal to the relevant Autocall Barrier, the product will be redeemed  on  the  corresponding  Early  Redemption  Date.  You  will  receive  for  each certificate a payment in cash equal to the Notional Amount\\n\\n- seek to invest in an income paying product, potentially to diversify their portfolio.\\n- are able to bear losses up to the total of the Notional Amount and are aware of the possible early termination of the product.\\n- have been informed or have sufficient knowledge of the financial markets, their functioning and their risks, and the asset class of the underlying.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE RISKS AND WHAT COULD I GET IN RETURN?\\n\\n## RISK INDICATOR\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\nThe risk indicator assumes you keep the product for 5 years. The actual risk can vary significantly if you cash in at an early stage and you may get back less. You may not be able to sell your product easily or you may have to sell at a price that significantly impacts on how much you get back.\\n\\nThe summary risk indicator (SRI) is a guide to the level of risk of this product compared to other products. It shows how likely it is that the product will lose money because of movements in the markets or because we are not able to pay you.\\n\\nWe have classified this product as 4 out of 7, which is a medium risk class.\\n\\nThis rates the potential losses from future performance at a medium level, and poor market conditions are very unlikely to impact our capacity to pay you.\\n\\nYou will receive payments in the product's currency, which may be different from your domestic currency. In this case, be aware of currency risk . The final return you will get depends on the exchange rate between the two currencies. This risk is not considered in the indicator shown above.\\n\\nThis product does not include any protection from future market performance so you could lose some or all of your investment.\\n\\nIf we are not able to pay you what is owed, you could lose your entire investment.\\n\\nFor detailed information about all risks please refer to the risk sections of the legal documentation as specified in the section 'Other relevant information' below.\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE SCENARIOS\\n\\nWhat you will get from this product depends on future market performance. Market developments in the future are uncertain and cannot be accurately predicted.\\n\\nThe scenarios shown are illustrations based on results from the past and on certain assumptions. Markets could develop very differently in the future.\\n\\n| Recommended Holding Period  Until the product is called or matures.  This may be different in each scenario and is indicated in the table.  Example Investment  USD 10,000  Scenarios  If you exit after 1 year  If you exit at call or  maturity  Minimum  USD 2,520. The return is only guaranteed if you hold the product to maturity.  Stress scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 3,613  USD 5,006  (product ends after 13 December  2027)  Average return each year  -63.87%  -28.95%  Unfavourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 8,139  USD 6,779  (product ends after 13 December  2027)  Average return each year  -18.61%  -17.47%  Moderate scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 11,260  (product ends after 04 December  2026)  Average return each year  12.6%  Favourable scenario  What you might get back after costs  USD 11,259  USD 12,205  (product ends after 02 September  2027)  Average return each year  12.59%  12.09%   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nThe figures shown include all the costs of the product itself, but may not include all the costs that you pay to your advisor or distributor. The figures do not take into account your personal tax situation, which may also affect how much you get back.\\n\\nThe stress scenario shows what you might get back in extreme market circumstances.\\n\\nThe favourable, moderate and unfavourable scenarios represent possible outcomes, which have been calculated based on simulations using the reference assets' past performance over up to 5 past years.\\n\\nThis product cannot be easily cashed in. If you exit the investment earlier than the recommended holding period you do not have a guarantee and you may have to pay extra costs.\\n\\n## WHAT HAPPENS IF THE MANUFACTURER IS UNABLE TO PAY OUT?\\n\\nShould the Issuer default or file for bankruptcy, you have the right to seek payment from the Guarantor pursuant to an unconditional and irrevocable guarantee of any amount due. Should the Guarantor also default, file for bankruptcy or in case of bail-in, you may suffer a loss up to the total amount invested.\\n\\nThe product is not covered by any statutory investor compensation or guarantee scheme.\\n\\nInvestors should note that BNP Paribas, acting as Guarantor, is licensed as a credit institution in France and as such is subject to the resolution regime introduced by the EU Bank Recovery and Resolution Directive of 15 May 2014. This regulation, among others, gives resolution authorities the power to amend the key terms of the guarantee, to reduce the amounts payable by the Guarantor under the terms of the guarantee (including a possible reduction to zero) and to convert the amounts due under the guarantee into shares or other securities or other obligations of the Guarantor. Restructuring may be imposed by resolution authorities to avoid bankruptcy. Investors may not be able to recover all or even part of the amount due under the product (if any) from the Guarantor under the guarantee or may receive a different security issued by the Guarantor in place of the amount (if any) due to the Investors under the product by the Issuer, which may be worth significantly less than the amount due to investors under the product at maturity.\\n\\n## WHAT ARE THE COSTS?\\n\\nThe person advising on or selling you this product may charge you other costs. If so, this person will provide you with information about these costs and how they affect your investment.\\n\\n## COSTS OVER TIME\\n\\nThe tables show the amounts that are taken from your investment to cover different types of costs. These amounts depend on how much you invest, how long you hold the product and how well the product does. The amounts shown here are illustrations based on an example investment amount and different possible investment periods:\\n\\nThe duration of this product is uncertain as it may terminate at different times depending on how the market evolves. The amounts shown here consider two different scenarios (early call and maturity). In case you decide to exit before the product ends, exit costs may apply in addition to the amounts shown here.\\n\\nWe have assumed:\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n- USD 10,000 is invested\\n- A performance of the product that is consistent with each holding period shown.\\n\\n| Investment USD 10,000  Scenarios  If the product is called at the first possible date 04  December 2026  If the product reaches maturity  Total costs  USD 210  USD 210  Annual cost impact (*)  2.42%  1.12%   |\\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\nWe may share part of the costs with the person selling you the product to cover the services they provide to you. They will inform you of the amount.\\n\\n## COMPOSITION OF COSTS\\n\\n| One-off costs upon entry or exit  If you exit after 1 year  Entry costs  2.1% of the amount you pay in when entering this investment.  These costs are already included in the price you pay.  USD 210  Exit costs  0.5%. These costs only apply if you exit your investment prior to the maturity of the product. The number  indicated assumes that normal market conditions applies.  USD 50  Ongoing costs taken each year  Management fees and other  administrative or operating costs  0% of the notional of your investment per year.  USD 0  Transaction costs  0%  USD 0  Incidental costs taken under specific conditions  Performance fees  There is no performance fee for this product.  USD 0   |\\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\\n\\n## HOW LONG SHOULD I HOLD IT AND CAN I TAKE MY MONEY OUT EARLY?\\n\\nRecommended holding period: until 13 December 2027, which corresponds to the product's maturity.\\n\\nHowever the duration of the product is not known in advance as it may be redeemed early.\\n\\nThe objective of the product is to provide you with the redemption profile described under \\"What is this product?\\" above. This only applies if the product is held until maturity.\\n\\nUnder normal market conditions, you may sell this product in the secondary market, at a price depending on the markets parameters prevailing at the time, which could put the invested amount at risk. Should you decide to resell, a fee of 0.50% will be deducted from the market price which could be increased under specific market condition.\\n\\nThe 0.50% commission has been taken into account in the table. In addition, the distributor may charge additional costs in the event of an exit before the maturity.\\n\\n## HOW CAN I COMPLAIN?\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the conduct of the person advising on or selling the product can be submitted directly to that person.\\n\\nAny complaint regarding the product can be submitted by writing to the following address: BNP Paribas CLM Regulations - Client Engagement and Protection Regulations - Torre Ocidente Rua Galileu Galilei, 2, 13º, 1500-392, Lisboa, PORTUGAL, by sending an e-mail to cib.priips.complaints@bnpparibas.com, or by using the online form available at the following website https://kid.bnpparibas.com/cib/claim.\\n\\n## OTHER RELEVANT INFORMATION\\n\\nThe information contained in this Key Information Document does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell the product and is no substitute for individual consultation with your bank or advisor.\\n\\nFor a further information on the product, including the risks involved, you should read the related legal documentation (prospectus / base prospectus and any supplement, and final terms), which is available free of charge from your financial advisor.\\n\\nThis product may not be offered or sold, directly or indirectly, in the United States of America or to U.S. persons. The term \\"U.S. person\\" is defined in Regulation S under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933 (Securities Act). The offering of this product has not been registered under the Securities Act.\\n\\n<!-- image -->\\n\\n## Coupon\\n\\n| Coupon Payment Date(s)  Coupon Rate(s)  06 January 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  03 February 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  05 March 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  02 April 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  04 May 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  03 June 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  06 July 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  03 August 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  02 September 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  05 October 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  02 November 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  04 December 2026  1.05% of the Notional Amount  06 January 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  02 February 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  05 March 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  02 April 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  03 May 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  03 June 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  06 July 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  02 August 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  02 September 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  04 October 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  02 November 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount  13 December 2027  1.05% of the Notional Amount   |\\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------